there is no port listening on 7000, which is the port you are trying to expose via the Kubernetes NodePort service. \par
\b Steps to Resolve:\b0\par
1. Update Kubernetes Service to Match the Correct Port\par
If your application is indeed listening on port 3000 (as per the netstat output), you need to expose the correct port using Kubernetes kubectl expose:\par
\cf1\par
kubectl delete svc ems-ui-service\par
\par
\b\f0\fs22  \cf4 f your application is indeed listening on port 3000 (as per the netstat output), you need to expose the correct port using Kubernetes kubectl expose\cf1 :\par
\cf0\b0\f1\fs18  \cf1 kubectl expose pod ems-app-pod --port=3000 --target-port=3000 --name=ems-ui-service --type=NodePort\par
\cf4 This will create a service exposing port 3000\f2\lang2057 ,The NodePort will automatically be assigned (or you can specify it manually, such as --node-port=30401).\f1\lang9\par
